*.sage.py

# Signing keys and certificates. `.p8` in particular is the APNs auth key: it is
# downloadable from Apple exactly ONCE, never expires, and grants push for every app
# on the team — so a commit is both unrecoverable and high-impact. The backend reads
# it from the APNS_AUTH_KEY env var (contents, not a path) precisely so it never has
# to live in the repo.
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.cer

# Environments
.env
# The bare `.env` above does NOT cover siblings — `.env.bak`, `.env.local` and
# `.env.production` were all committable until 2026-08-15. That is exactly the shape of an
# accidental secret commit: you back up `.env` before a key rotation and the backup, holding
# the key you just retired, is untracked-but-not-ignored and gets swept into `git add -A`.
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

